          }
        ],
        "publish_places": [
          "Garden City"
        ],
        "first_sentence": {
          "type": "/type/text",
          "value": "Two events occurred in 1908 that were to be of lasting significance in the progress of the automobile industry: William C. Durant, working from his base in the Buick Motor Company, formed the General Motors Company-predecessor of the present General Motors Corporation-and Henry Ford announced the Model T."
        },
